 "notes": [
  "The roof skin of Galvanised corrugated steel sheet, weathered is under 3 mm of metal and conducts almost nothing away, so it sets only the surface optics and is left out of the solid mesh.",
  "Sun absorbed in the glass and passed into the room, 173 kWh, is taken from EnergyPlus's window heat balance and added at the air node; MAPDL computes the window's conduction itself.",
  "Partition walls inside the room, which EnergyPlus carries as internal mass, are not in the MAPDL mesh."
 ],
 "sources": [
  {
   "citation": "Inside surface coefficients of ISO 6946 Annex C: convection 2.5 W/m2K on walls, 5.0 for heat flowing up through the roof and 0.7 down through the floor, and long wave radiation 0.9 x 5.7 W/m2K; outside convection 4 + 4v W/m2K with v the wind speed and linearised long wave radiation to the sky",
   "status": "derived",
   "url": null,
   "note": "Convection joins each surface to the room air and radiation joins it to a radiant star node, the two node room model of ISO 52016, in place of EnergyPlus's view factor exchange between every pair of surfaces."
